            "review_title": "Review at Gogi House - Saigon Centre",
            "review_text": "Rob Nesbit\nWarsaw, Poland6958 contributions\n7\nRecommended.\nNov 2022\nMeat extravaganza, yes another one!\nWasn't expecting much when I sat down, as places in malls tend to be a bit drab and unexciting.\nOrdered from a touchscreen device which was handy and easy to use.......\nFood came quick and fast and we were off cooking our own variety of meats we had ordered. And a egg rice dish and some soup to accompany, and also the usual beers and juices one has to water it all down!\nThe food was great, very succulent and well prepped, slender and juicy, delicious. The egg rice dish was so nice we ordered another one. For after's my friend got some ice cream, a few goes of it, she really liked it.....\nOverall the food was great, and the service very good, cleaning our table of plates quickly and with a smile.\nMeal came to about 40 Euros, a teeny bit pricey but for the amount we ate, not bad.\nRecommended.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 7, 2022",
